note The node font's cell width and row height at the current zoom and the pixel padding inside a node (half a cell). Layout happens in cells and rows; the scene turns it into pixels with these, so zooming scales positions by the factor the text really grew by, not by the nominal zoom. The spacing constants are in cells too (Spacing).

