note The one entry, called from App::graph_layout after Built::measure has written every size. It groups the nodes by rank, clears last frame's sibling boxes, lays out the lanes along the main axis, builds the forest, then places the roots as their top-level boxes (top_siblings) and walks breadth first from all of them together, each node's callee-side children and then its caller-side children that are not placed yet becoming one sibling box beside it (place_siblings). The done set places a node reachable from two parents only once, under the first. It writes one CellPoint per node into position and one Siblings per box into siblings.

