note The gaps for one direction, in cells: rank_gap between lanes, sibling_gap between the members of a box, box_gap between boxes in a lane, the lead before a box's first member along each axis (lead_main, lead_cross: the box header's rows on whichever axis runs down, the padding on the other) and the padding after it (pad_main, pad_cross). Left to right the lanes are columns and the cross axis is rows, so the gaps come from the ACROSS and DOWN constants accordingly.

